{
  "scenario_name": "renderer_parity_mp_constant_noise_smoke",
  "description": "2.0 renderer parity experiment (Workbench D-041): the same run as renderer_parity_mp_smoke with --debug-renderer-constant-noise, which gives the combiner's noise term frame count 0 and noise scale 0 in both backends, so its random() returns exactly 0 (noise input 0.5; the dithered alpha test keeps only opaque texels). Differences that remain do not come from the noise hash. 2.0 renderer phase 2a (D5): renderer parity (see renderer_parity_menu_smoke) in a Combat Simulator match on Felicity with two simulants, one placed in view, first person with the match HUD. Three captures after offline gameplay is ready, on the virtual timeline.",
